  "releaseNotes": "v2.0.4 - Connection/transaction lifecycle: AddRangeSync commits before disconnect; Commit/Cancel no longer flip keepConnection; CompositeCommand attaches live transactions only; PersistComposition honors keep-alive. [FIX] cluster replication wrote back to master (loop ignored its connection string — replicas never received data). Dependency refresh: Dapper 2.1.79 -> 2.1.89; Microsoft.Data.Sqlite 9.0.18 -> 10.0.12; Microsoft.Data.SqlClient 6.1.1 -> 7.1.0; System.Text.Json 9.0.18 -> 10.0.12; MySqlConnector 2.6.1 -> 2.6.2; Rochas.BWOQ 1.6.6 -> 1.6.8 (package icon); Rochas.SqlWrapper 1.4.9 -> 1.5.0 (statement cache, dotless-namespace fix — via NuGet). v2.0.3 - Rochas.SqlWrapper 1.4.8 -> 1.4.9 (DateOnly/TimeOnly as quoted ISO literals); Rochas.BWOQ 1.6.5 -> 1.6.6. v2.0.2 - Async/sync path separation: new FillCompositionAsync (no more sync-over-async hangs on cyclic compositions), truly-async paginated builder, path-based cycle guard with depth cap, paged queries now honor loadComposition, sync APIs run on sync executors; PostgreSQL inserts with client-generated keys skip lastval (55000 fallback); GuidStringHandler registered for all engines (TEXT Guid PKs on PG). v2.0.1 - Rochas.SqlWrapper 1.1.2 -> 1.4.8 (PostgreSQL-valid GROUP BY + EntityReflector with cache). v2.0.0 - [NEW] PostgreSQL support in CompositeCommand (parameterized Query/Search Paginate, Add, Update and Remove now run on Npgsql: null maps to DBNull, Guid maps to text following GuidStringHandler); test project now consumes Rochas.CacheIndexer 1.1.0 from NuGet instead of a local ProjectReference. v1.9.8 - Contracts moved to Rochas.Data.Specification (DataSpecification), replacing the internal Rochas.DapperRepository.Specification project.",
